License: MIT or Apache-2.0, and others
 The crates from crates.io that Laccy is built with, bundled because
 Launchpad builds without network access. Each crate states its license in
 its Cargo.toml and license files. For Laccy 0.1.6 they are under MIT,
 Apache-2.0 or both, except foldhash (Zlib), target-lexicon
 (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), one crate under Unlicense OR MIT and
 one that adds Unicode-3.0. libsqlite3-sys bundles SQLite, which is in the
 public domain.
 .
 On Debian and Ubuntu systems, the full text of the Apache License 2.0 is
 in /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0.

